   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&#x2019; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The National Trade Union Council (NTUC) and its membership organizations agreed to reform the NTUC into workers&apos; platforms to better advocate workers&#x2019; views and positions to the Government and employers. The vision and mission statement on this was endorsed at a meeting in December 2022. Following this statement, a five-year strategic plan was adopted at the end of 2023.  

In December 2022 the NTUC provided input to the Ministry of Labour and Vocational Training (MLVT) regarding the draft TVET Law of Cambodia. MLVT acknowledged the inputs and indicated the inputs will be elaborated in the TVET Law. 

A framework agreement to establish a bipartite forum with the Cambodian Federation of Employers and Business Associations (CAMFEBA) was signed in September 2023.

NTUC&apos;s priorities for decent work in Cambodia were reflected in the Global Accelerator roadmap.  The same roadmap was presented by the Cambodian Prime Minister at the SDGs Summit at the UN in September 2023. ILO provided technical support and advice to NTUC and its organizations using ACTRAV materials such as &apos;Trade Union in the Balance&apos;,  that strengthen its capacity to organize workers including workers from emerging sectors. 

With support from the ILO-China Partnership Program, the ILO organized a workshop in December 2022 to provide technical support to draft the input to the TVET Law of Cambodia.

With the support of the Japanese Government, the ILO assisted the social partners in developing an agreement to establish a bipartite forum. To this effect, a preparatory meeting was held in May 2023 where NTUC representatives identified priorities that needed to be discussed with representatives of the Cambodian Federation of Employers and Business Associations (CAMFEBA).</narrative>
   </description>
